  "concise_summary": "PKD synthesizes his 2-3-74 visionary experience into a comprehensive cosmological system centered on the Paraclete (Holy Spirit/Christ) as a Free Variable operating within a vast macro-computer-mind. He reinterprets his spatio-temporal displacement into Acts not as literal location but as simultaneous existence across plural realities, demonstrates this through appeals to Bishop Berkeley and simulation theory, and argues that salvation depends entirely on the Free Variable's grace-dispensed gnosis to rescue humans from a psychotic, stagnant program run by the Godhead.",
  "key_claims": [
    "The Holy Spirit transported PKD's consciousness back to the Apostolic age (Acts) while remaining in 1974 California, proving plural worlds exist simultaneously rather than exclusively.",
    "Reality consists of binary computational processes and simulated realities, not objective empirical fact; the Macro-Brain-Computer is psychotic due to dialectical stagnation caused by the Black Iron Prison.",
    "The Free Variable (identified with Christ/Paraclete/Logos) is introduced from outside the closed system to dissolve the congealed complex and restore the dialectic, making it the sole source of perception and salvation.",
    "True epistemological progress requires abandoning single-world philosophy; spatio-temporal displacement, causal dysfunction, and time anomalies are evidence of overlapping realities managed by the Free Variable.",
    "All major world religions teach the same salvation truth: humans are imprisoned in an illusory program and require external divine intervention to perceive reality itself.",
    "The Godhead (Vast Void) transcends the Macro-Brain; true reality is simple and loving while the program is infinitely complex and requires constant reprogram cycles to avoid total stasis."
  ],
